                <pb facs="0819" n="805" xml:id="pg805"/>

                <head><seg type="margin">[92]</seg> *<hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Field, Acting Attorney-General, to Mr. Barlow, United States marshal.</hi></head>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1869-07-03"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 3,
                        1869</date>.</dateline>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis C. Barlow</hi>, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">United States Marshal, New York:</hi></p>
                <p>The officers and men must be put in judicial custody as soon as possible, either
                    under separate or joint complaints j and if a writ of <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >habeas corpus</hi> issues before they are arrested on a warrant, pending
                    the hearing of the writ, a warrant can be obtained, and immediately served, if
                    they are discharged at the hearing.</p>
                <p>Give copy to district attorney.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. A. FIELD,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting-Attorney
                        General.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
